# Build-context exclusions for `docker build` (local + Bitbucket Pipelines).
# Keeps the cloud build context small and ensures no local-only / sensitive
# material ever lands in an image layer. Dependencies and build outputs are
# regenerated inside the Dockerfiles, so they must NOT be copied in.

# VCS + tooling
.git
.gitignore
# NOTE: do NOT blanket-exclude *.md — backend/prompts/*.md are loaded at
# runtime and docs/user-manual/*.md are synced into the frontend and bundled by
# Vite (?raw) at build time (see frontend/scripts/sync-manual.mjs). Excluding
# them breaks the image builds.

# Local Claude Code session state + any local reference material
.claude
docs/Claude CRA Analysis Reference

# Dependencies (reinstalled in-image)
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (rebuilt in-image)
backend/dist
frontend/dist

# Env + secrets (never baked into an image)
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Runtime/working data that may exist on a dev machine
clones
artifacts
backups
*.log

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
